# --- GPL-3.0 fetched samples (copyleft - never committed into this MIT repo) ---
# These files are downloaded on demand by the fetch_sample.sh script in the
# relevant technique folder. They exist locally for rule testing but are kept
# out of git to avoid mixing GPL-3.0 content into Carlos's MIT-licensed repo.
# See the corresponding logs/<technique>/SOURCE.md for the reasoning.
logs/T1059.001_powershell/exec_emotet_ps_4104.evtx
*.evtx

# --- Large MIT fetched samples (excluded for REPO SIZE, not licensing) ---
# These OTRF/Security-Datasets logs are MIT-licensed, so vendoring them would
# be license-fine - they are kept out of git purely because they are large
# (~20 MB / ~41 MB / ~80 MB) and would bloat the history of every clone. Each
# is downloaded on demand by its technique folder's fetch_sample.sh, which
# verifies the extracted file against a pinned sha256 so it is byte-identical
# to what results/ and screenshots/ were built from. See the corresponding
# logs/<technique>/SOURCE.md for the reasoning.
logs/T1021.002_smb_admin_shares/empire_smbexec_dcerpc_smb_svcctl_2020-09-20025716.json
logs/T1055_process_injection/empire_psinject_PEinjection_2020-08-07143205.json
logs/T1547.001_registry_run_keys/empire_persistence_registry_modification_run_keys_standard_user_2020-09-04030609.json

